# Ask the official z1_ctrl process to enter one of its finite state machine
# states.
#
# Only the states this component can actually drive are accepted:
#
#   PASSIVE|JOINTCTRL|BACKTOSTART|CALIBRATION|TOSTATE|SAVESTATE|TEACH|TEACHREPEAT
#
# CARTESIAN, MOVEJ, MOVEL, MOVEC, TRAJECTORY and LOWCMD are refused, with the
# reason in `message`: they read valueUnion as a posture, a trajectory or raw
# motor commands, and ros2_control only ever fills in joint positions. See
# z1_ros2_control/README.md.

# State name, case-insensitive.
string state

# Label for the states that z1_ctrl addresses by name - it looks the label up in
# its config/savedArmStates.csv. Required (and at most 9 characters) for
# TOSTATE, SAVESTATE, TEACH and TEACHREPEAT; must be empty for the others.
string label
---
bool success

# Why the request failed, or what z1_ctrl acknowledged when it succeeded.
string message

# What z1_ctrl reported by the time this call returned, whether it succeeded or
# not. This is the same value as get_fsm_state would report.
string current_state
